                        "name": "Ethan Wei",
                        "email": "ethanwei@ami.com",
                        "username": "ethanweiTW"
                    },
                    "message": "There's one IPv4 address and its address source showing via IPMI command. So, If there are more than one IPv4 address under one interface, the result may confuses the users and regard it as an incorrect response."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 8,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ravi Teja",
                        "email": "raviteja28031990@gmail.com",
                        "username": "raviteja-b"
                    },
                    "message": "I understand the problem but this fix does not fix this issue completely.\nto avoid this issue, networkd need to put checks to avoid allowing multiple IP configuration."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 8,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ethan Wei",
                        "email": "ethanwei@ami.com",
                        "username": "ethanweiTW"
                    },
                    "message": "The first step I want is to avoid confuseing the users when getting LAN configuration via IPMI commands. Although multiple IPs can be set under one interface, if possible, I'd like to put checks avoid the second IP under one interface. Thanks."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ravi Teja",
                        "email": "raviteja28031990@gmail.com",
                        "username": "raviteja-b"
                    },
                    "message": "Looking for reply on outstanding comments."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/ethernet_interface.cpp",
                    "line": 834,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ravi Teja",
                        "email": "raviteja28031990@gmail.com",
                        "username": "raviteja-b"
                    },
                    "message": "IPv6 supports multiple addresses per interface by default and DHCPv6 & static v6 addresses can coexist on interface.\nwhat's the issue noticed with ipv6 dhcp & static address co-existence?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/ethernet_interface.cpp",
                    "line": 834,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ethan Wei",
                        "email": "ethanwei@ami.com",
                        "username": "ethanweiTW"
                    },
                    "message": "We noticed it couldn't establich connection if other device had already applied the same IPv6 address."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/ethernet_interface.cpp",
                    "line": 834,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ravi Teja",
                        "email": "raviteja28031990@gmail.com",
                        "username": "raviteja-b"
                    },
                    "message": "yeah you can't have same ip address on multiple devices.\nplease try configuring unique ip which is not configured on other devices"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/ethernet_interface.cpp",
                    "line": 834,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ethan Wei",
                        "email": "ethanwei@ami.com",
                        "username": "ethanweiTW"
                    },
                    "message": "I will remove the checks for IPv6. Thanks."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/ethernet_interface.cpp",
                    "line": 836,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ravi Teja",
